120 high)", "always_in": "long", "notes": "H4 context (current, decision_time_ms 1789991999999) and D1 context (current, decision_time_ms 1789948799999) both read bull-trend/breakout-spike; D1 context is used only for the 2771 spike-high location, and raw closed M15/H1 bars are the entry evidence."}, "setup": {"type": "breakout pullback: buy the breakout of the 21-bar M15 tight range that has held above the broken 2700 H4 double top", "trigger_status": "pending", "signal_quality": "weak", "location_assessment": "neutral", "no_trade_reason": null}, "decision_timeframe": "M15", "context_timeframes_used": ["H1", "M15", "H4", "D1"], "entry_mechanism": "breakout_pullback", "trigger": {"reference": "M15 bar 119 high (range high)", "price_field": "high", "price": "2747.76", "source": {"timeframe": "M15", "bar_index": 119, "open_time_ms": 1790001900000, "close_time_ms": 1790002799999}, "kind": "stop", "direction": "above"}, "invalidation": {"reference": "M15 bar 117 low (low of the recent higher-low cluster 2718.09/2720.15/2718.23; back into the middle of the tight range)", "price_field": "low", "price": "2718.09", "source": {"timeframe": "M15", "bar_index": 117, "open_time_ms": 1790000100000, "close_time_ms": 1790000999999}}, "evidence_for": ["M15 bar 119 (open 2733.06, close 2734.92) is the highest close of the 21-bar consolidation and takes out the prior range highs: 2739.54 (bar 112), 2741.55 (bar 115), 2742.56 (bar 118), then 2747.76 (bar 119) - range highs are rising into the close.", "The M15 range since the spike bar 98 (open 2708.33, high 2850, low 2702.56, close 2739.13) has held entirely above 2702.56, i.e. above the H4 2700 zone that had been tagged twice (H4 bar 108 high 2700, H4 bar 118 high 2700) - a tight consolidation above a broken double top, not a pullback below it.", "H1 follow-through per the H4 transition condition: H1 bars 117-119 (open_time 1789992000000 / 1789995600000 / 1789999200000) closed 2734.09, 2734.13, 2734.92, all above the H4 breakout bar's close 2723.15, with lows 2719.08 / 2720.15 / 2718.09 above 2700.", "H1 bar 119 (open 2734.63, high 2747.76, low 2718.09, close 2734.92) makes a higher high versus H1 bar 118 high 2741.55 and closes at the top of the last five H1 bars (lows 2709.56, 2713.04, 2719.08, 2720.15, 2718.09 all hold above 2700).", "M15 lows have stopped falling under the range: 2718.23 (bar 116), 2718.09 (bar 117), 2731.83 (bar 118), 2731.83 (bar 119), so a stop below 2718.09 is a defensible structural invalidation with a defined 29.67-point risk from the 2747.76 trigger."], "evidence_against": ["M15 bar 98 printed 2850 and closed 2739.13, a 147.44-point bar with a 110.87-point upper tail; the whole 21-bar range sits inside that tail, so the buy trigger 2747.76 is still 102.24 below a level that was just rejected.", "H4 bar 120 (open 2658.81, high 2850, low 2658.06, close 2723.15) left a 126.85-point upper tail with no follow-through bar in the window; the H4 context flags two earlier upside spikes (bar 61 high 2680, bar 81 high 2609.02) that were fully retraced.", "Overhead structure crowds the setup versus its invalidation: 2747.76 is only 5.20 above the prior M15 range high 2742.56 and only 23.24 below the 2771 D1 spike high, against a 29.67-point stop distance.", "Bar 119 is a weak breakout bar, not a bull trend bar closing on its high: its close 2734.92 sits in the lower ~19% of its 2731.83-2747.76 range with a 12.84 upper tail.", "The 21-bar M15 range is only about 45 points (1.6%) and oscillates around the H4 breakout bar's close 2723.15 - consistent with balance at the breakout level, and tight-range breakouts frequently fail without a strong breakout bar."], "qualitative_confidence": "medium", "uncertainty": ["Whether the M15 tight range resolves upward or becomes a final flag: no bar in the supplied packet closes above 2747.76, so the breakout is untriggered and unconfirmed.", "The would-be signal bar is already printed (bar 119) and is marginal (new high by 5.20 with a 12.84 upper tail); a stronger bull bar closing on its high would raise confidence in the same trigger.", "The D1 context is 15 hours older than the frozen decision time and its 2771/2557 levels are contextual descriptions; the D1 spike high 2771 was exceeded only by a wick (M15 bar 98 high 2850) with no close above it."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["A M15 close back below 2731.83 (bar 119 low) and then below 2718.09 (bar 117 low) would mark a failed breakout of the range high and void the long case.", "A M15/H1 close below 2702.56 (bar 98 low) would break the three-hour acceptance above the H4 2700 zone and return price to the prior H4 wide range.", "Repeated M15 closes between 2718.09 and 2747.76 without exceeding 2747.76 would keep the tight-range read and argue against a breakout.", "A M15 close above 2747.76 with the low holding above 2731.83 would confirm the breakout and shift the focus to 2771 and then 2850."]}, "latest_trader_intent": {"schema": "brooks.trade-intent.v2", "role": "TRADER", "decision": "ENTER_LONG", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1790027999999, "market_context": {"regime": "bull trend on H1/H4/D1; M15 bull leg pausing in a two-sided pullback that still holds above the last breakout shelf", "h4": "context freshness current: bull-trend / breakout-spike above the 2700.00 equal highs (bars 106/116) with spike high 2850.00 on bar 118 (upper tail 126.85 = 66% of its 191.94 range) and contracting bars 119-120 (76.91, 35.81) that stop below 2850.00; possible buy-climax shape, no bear reversal bar printed yet", "h1": "bull trend with rising lows 2646.02 -> 2658.06 -> 2694.94 -> 2709.56 -> 2718.09 -> 2737.86 -> 2762.93; last H1 bar (open_time_ms 1790024400000) is a bear bar open 2781.77, high 2782.00, low 2762.93, close 2768.10 after the bull bar open 2760.51, high 2804.59, close 2781.77", "m15": "bull leg 2734.22 (bar 103 low) to 2804.59 (bar 113 high); six-bar pullback to 2762.93 (bar 117 low) holding above the 2746.20-2756.72 shelf (bar 111 low 2746.20, bar 111 high 2756.72, bar 107 close 2756.61); last bar 119 open 2776.18, high 2776.18, low 2768.10, close 2768.10", "levels": {"resistance": ["2804.59", "2850.00"], "support": ["2762.93", "2746.20", "2734.22", "2718.09"]}}, "setup": {"type": "bull-trend pullback continuation: buy stop above M15 bull signal bar 118 high", "trigger_status": "pending", "signal_quality": "weak", "location_assessment": "neutral", "no_trade_reason": null}, "decision_timeframe": "M15", "context_timeframes_used": ["H4", "H1", "M15"], "entry_mechanism": "continuation", "trigger": {"reference": "M15 bar 118 (bull signal bar, close in top quarter of range) high", "price_field": "high", "price": "2779.05", "source": {"timeframe": "M15", "bar_index": 118, "open_time_ms": 1790026200000, "close_time_ms": 1790027099999}, "kind": "stop", "direction": "above"}, "invalidation": {"reference": "M15 bar 117 low (pullback low / breakout-test low)", "price_field": "low", "price": "2762.93", "source": {"timeframe": "M15", "bar_index": 117, "open_time_ms": 1790025300000, "close_time_ms": 1790026199999}}, "evidence_for": ["Higher-timeframe trend agrees with the long: H4 context (freshness current) is bull-trend/breakout-spike with bars 113-120 closing 2577.69 to 2760.51 (seven of eight closes higher) and the 2700.00 equal highs of H4 bars 106/116 exceeded (closes 2723.15, 2754.31, 2760.51).", "M15 sequence of higher lows is intact: 2718.09 (bar 89 low), 2730.01 (bar 95 low), 2734.22 (bar 103 low), 2762.93 (bar 117 low), so the current pullback has not broken the bull leg structure.", "The six-bar M15 pullback off 2804.59 (bar 113 high) is holding above the prior breakout shelf 2746.20-2756.72 (bar 111 low 2746.20, high 2756.72; bar 107 close 2756.61), i.e. a breakout test rather than a broken trend.", "M15 bar 118 is a bull reversal bar (open 2768.60, low 2768.42, high 2779.05, close 2776.18) closing in the top quarter of its range and above bar 117's high 2769.23, giving a specific pending stop (2779.05) with structural risk only 16.12 below it at 2762.93."], "evidence_against": ["M15 bar 113 (open 2771.06, high 2804.59, close 2803.78, range 34.81, widest of the leg) broke the bar 95 high 2795.00 by only 9.59 and was fully retraced in three bars to 2767.94 (bar 116 low) - a marginal new high that was immediately rejected.", "Last bar M15 bar 119 (open 2776.18 = its high, close 2768.10 = its low) is a bear bar closing at its low and takes out bar 118's low 2768.42, so buyers lost the most recent bar and a deeper second leg toward 2746.20/2734.22 is possible.", "Location is only neutral: 2768 is near the middle of the M15 range 2718.09-2804.59 (mid ~2761) and about 25 points under the 2804.59 high, so reward to first resistance is roughly 1.6x the 16.12-point risk.", "H4 context flags possible buy-climax character overhead: H4 bar 118 range 191.94 with a 126.85 (66%) upper tail to 2850.00, and H4 bars 119-120 contract (76.91, 35.81) with highs 2795.00 and 2770.03 below 2850.00, so supply sits just above the trigger.", "Three consecutive M15 bear bars (114, 115, 116: closes 2783.49, 2781.77, 2768.05) mean the first bull attempt after the leg down already failed, and a High 2 buy could print lower, near 2762.93-2747, rather than the 2779.05 stop triggering."], "qualitative_confidence": "medium", "uncertainty": ["Whether this is a tradeable High 1/High 2 pullback or the start of a broader M15 trading range 2734.22-2804.59: bar 119 already took out bar 118's low 2768.42, so the pending 2779.05 stop may simply not fill while price works lower to 2762.93-2747.", "The H4 buy-climax shape at 2850.00 is unresolved (no bear reversal bar printed), so a bull leg resuming could still stall at 2804.59/2850.00.", "H1 and H4 contexts are directional labels; the raw H4 bar 118 upper tail shows the 2850.00 spike was sold, so the higher-timeframe leg may be shifting from spike to channel or range rather than extending."], "conditions_that_change_market_read": ["A close below M15 bar 117 low 2762.93 - and above all a close below bar 111 low 2746.20 - invalidates the continuation read and shifts M15 to a deeper pullback / trading range.", "A close above 2804.59 (bar 113 high) with follow-through confirms continuation toward the H4 spike high 2850.00; rejection there with a bear reversal bar would validate the H4 buy-climax read instead.", "Two consecutive M15 closes below 2734.22 (bar 103 low) break the sequence of rising M15 lows and end the bull-leg read.", "A M15 bull bar closing in its upper third above 2769.23, holding above 2762.93, would confirm the pullback is over rather than two-sided."]}, "latest_market_context": {"schema": "brooks.market-context.v1", "role": "HTF_ANALYST", "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "decision_time_ms": 1789948799999, "timeframe": "D1", "observations": ["Window opens at 2116.86 and falls to 1368.42 (bar 13 low, close 1568.55), then reverses; final close 2642.90 is about +24.9% versus the first open and about +93% above the window low.", "Bars 87-89 are the spike: 1916.51 to 2252.16, 2252.20 to 2326.32, 2326.31 to 2515.30, with the window high 2771 printed on bar 89.", "Bars 90-116 are two-sided: overlapping bodies, highs at 2557.46 (bar 95) and 2609.02 (bar 113), lows clustered 2357.18-2425.44; bar 110 spiked to 2680 and closed 2514.72 back inside the range.", "Bars 117-119 close 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 \u2014 the first consecutive closes above the 2557.46 ceiling; bar 117 has open 2446.22, high 2643.52, low 2436.87, range 206.65, closing in its top quarter; bar 118 reaches 2700.", "Bar 119 (open 2632.98, high 2645.88, low 2568.16, close 2642.90) is a 77.72-range bar closing near its high while holding above the range ceiling; it makes a lower high than bar 118 (2645.88 vs 2700).", "Recent lows rise: 2357.18 (bar 101), 2358.62 (bar 114), 2370.54 (bar 115), 2413.82 (bar 116), 2436.87 (bar 117), 2568.16 (bar 119).", "Price 2642.90 remains below the bar-89 spike high 2771, so the post-spike section is not yet a confirmed new-high trend."], "evidence_against": ["The breakout is only three bars; the preceding 27 bars overlap heavily and the region 2357-2557 can still be read as the operating trading range rather than broken.", "Two earlier upside probes failed to hold: bar 110 high 2680 closed 2514.72, bar 113 high 2609.02 closed 2514.07, so upside spikes in this region have recently been rejected.", "2642.90 remains below the bar-89 spike high 2771, so the whole post-spike section can be read as one broad trading range whose upper extreme has not been exceeded.", "Bar 119 makes a lower high than bar 118 (2645.88 vs 2700) with a lower tail to 2568.16, a pause rather than a strong continuation bar, and bar 114 had just traded down to 2358.62 four bars before the breakout."], "uncertainty": ["V2 D1 context adapted for the V1 PM input."]}, "management_history": [{"schema": "brooks.management-decision.v2", "role": "POSITION_MANAGER", "decision_time_ms": 1790013600000, "action": "HOLD", "position_ids": ["wf-main-5"], "reason": "The snapshot is coherent: one MAIN LONG leg (wf-main-5, 0.159) matches the executor mapping (wf-exec-9) and the single FILLED fill quantity (wf-fill-9), hedge_state is single_main with unresolved false and hedge_ratio 0, and margin_health is SAFE. management_policy sets strategy_stop_required false, so the empty open_orders list is policy-compliant, and the executor config still carries stop_price 2718.09 (the recorded M15 bar 117 invalidation low) with target 2812.14. The recorded premise (breakout-pullback long above the M15 range high 2747.76 with structural invalidation at 2718.09) is challenged but not contradicted: price took out 2747.76, spiked to 2795 and was rejected, and the last supplied M15 bars (1790012699999 close 2743.23 at its low; 1790013599999 open 2743.23, high 2743.61, low 2734.22, close 2740.89) drift back below the 2747.76 breakout level, yet every close still holds above the intent's stated failure trigger 2731.83 and well above the